Guarantee boundaries:
  LiveBytes is logical referenced file length, not physical occupancy.
  Fstatfs is an instantaneous shared-filesystem sample, not quota/reservation.
  UnconfirmedBytes is source offset minus last persisted GC confirmation,
  conservatively including already-applied but not locally confirmed records.
  GC remains ordered manifest-before-unlink; low admission watermark does not
  disable cold apply/GC. Real ENOSPC/fsync failures still poison the log.
  Explicit cleanup operates only in the dedicated owned namespace, preserves
  referenced/unknown/unsafe files and can retry after partial deletion.
  No automatic scheduling/reconnect, no production threshold/RPO choice,
  no TTL/eviction/warming/service wiring, no new hot-path throttling policy.

